node_modules/
dist/
app/dist/
# Vitest's coverage report — anchored to the root, because runs/coverage/ is
# the opposite of scratch: the filed coverage artifacts the findings cite.
/coverage/
# Playwright MCP's scratch output: screenshots, page snapshots and downloaded
# session records from a browser-driven walkthrough. Evidence for a review,
# never part of the record — the artifacts that count live in runs/.
.playwright-mcp/
*.log
.env
.env.*
# The template is the one .env file that is meant to be public: it carries the
# variable names and not one value.
!.env.example
# The dev-trace sink's output: the live page's dogfooding stream (model calls,
# prompts, latencies), appended by the vite dev server for an agent to tail.
# A debugging convenience, never a filed artifact — those live in runs/.
/.dev-trace.jsonl
